---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Settings · my-finances" active="settings">
  <header class="mb-6">
    <span class="eyebrow">Settings</span>
    <span class="accent-line"></span>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">Application settings</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="card p-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">About</h3>
    <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-2">
      The MEP rate is now fetched live from <code>api.argentinadatos.com</code> on every
      portfolio summary; the rate is displayed on the Portfolio page next to the
      "Last refresh" indicator. Other application settings (analysis model, prompt
      version, cost caps) live in the <code>portfolioSettings</code> table and can be
      edited via the API or Azure Storage Explorer.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card p-4 mt-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">Weekly macro context (feature 006)</h3>
    <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-2">
      The weekly analysis captures a macro panel, portfolio totals, and the week's
      position changes (shown on each analysis detail page). These are configured via
      <strong>App Settings / <code>local.settings.json</code></strong> (environment), not the
      settings table — the FRED key is a secret and MUST live there, never in source control:
    </p>
    <ul class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><code>analysis.fredApiKey</code> — free FRED API key (US CPI, Fed funds, S&amp;P 500).
        If absent, those indicators show as <em>unavailable</em>; the run still succeeds.</li>
      <li><code>analysis.imfModel</code> — model for the IMF news classification call
        (default <code>claude-haiku-4-5-20251001</code>).</li>
      <li><code>analysis.imfStalenessWeeks</code> — weeks before a carried-forward IMF status
        reverts to "unknown" (default <code>8</code>).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-muted)] mt-2">
      All other macro sources (riesgo país, FX gap, BCRA reserves/policy rate, AR inflation)
      are keyless and need no configuration.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
